# the Mach-O model to and from the neutral object
#
# to_neutral reads a relocatable Mach-O model into a neutral object through
# the naming rows and the relocation set of the file's architecture. what the
# neutral model has no field for travels in the object's facts, keyed by
# Mach-O, so the conversion back states what the file stated. from_neutral
# builds the Mach-O model of a neutral object, one segment of every section,
# its symbol and string tables and its load commands, for the writer to lay
# out.
#
# a section is named `segment,section`, its kind read from its type, name
# and flags, and its segment comes back from its name, or for a section that
# states none, from the layout class its flags and roles place it in. under
# MH_SUBSECTIONS_VIA_SYMBOLS every symbol starts an atom, a section is split
# for garbage collection, a symbol's size runs to the next symbol of its
# section, and a relocation that names a section resolves to the atom that
# holds its target. without the flag a section is one atom and such a
# relocation names a symbol standing for the section, which the conversion
# makes and the writer puts back as the section. the neutral symbols are the
# symbol table's entries in order, and a symbol the format has no entry for,
# a section's stand-in or a label with no name, is written as the section it
# lies in. a SUBTRACTOR record and the UNSIGNED record after it are one
# difference relocation, an ADDEND record is the addend of the record after
# it, and a SIGNED_n record keeps the bytes after its field in its addend.

